      "text": "Let's begin by identifying the radius of each circle.\n\nGiven that each circle is tangent to two sides of the square and its adjacent circles, we can deduce the side length of a single circle. Circles are diameters away from each other, and they are respectively tangent to one side and the opposite side.\n\nConsidering the geometry, the vertical distance between two adjacent circles is \\(r\\), and the horizontal distance is also \\(2r\\).\n\nSo, looking vertically at the diagram, the square side lengths are:\n\\[4 - 4r\\]\n\nHowever, since the circles are tangent vertically, the total length subtracted accounts for \\(2r\\) twice (since each side of the square is 4 segments).\n\nThus, we can write:\n\\[4 - 4r = 2r\\]\n\nNow let's solve this equation:\n\\[4 = 6r\\]\n\\[r = \\frac{2}{3}\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the semi-diagonal of the square:\n\\[\\frac{4-4r + 4}{2}\\]\n\nSimplify to get the radius of the circle:\n\\[R = \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{4-4r}{2}\\right)^2}\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(r = \\frac{2}{3}\\) we get;\n\\[R = \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{8}{2}\\right)^2}\\]\n\\[R = \\sqrt{4^2}\\]\n\\[4 - 4r = 2r\\]\n\nSubstituting r again:\nSolving for \\(r\\) again:\n\\[r = 1\\]\n\nSo, the shaded area is given by:\n\\[\\text{Shaded Area} = \\frac{\\pi r^2}{4} = \\frac{\\pi(1)^2}{4} = \\boxed{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}\\]\n\nFinally, we use the value of \\(\\pi\\) as 3.14 to get the numerical value of the shaded area.\n\nOur final answer:\n\\[\\text{Shaded Area}\\approx 7.85\\]\n\nSo, Wei will use approximately \\(7.85\\) square inches to cover the shaded area in the large square-shaped logo.",
